{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050397,"nonce":"rnW+pnBMLcfQYtjNnX5tVk3ciVM=","title":"POST /v1/secrets writes an Environment secret under an Environment name that does not exist","message":"`put_secret` (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs ~10137) writes an EnvironmentProject secret under any Environment name. It does not check that the Environment exists, and it needs only Administer on the Project.\n\nThis reopens the Duplicate window: a secret written under the new name while a Duplicate runs is overwritten if the Duplicate succeeds, and deleted by its cleanup if it fails. A PUT that creates the name already takes the Duplicate's claim (#102).\n\nOptions:\n- Refuse that scope for a missing Environment, or for one a Duplicate claims.\n- Have Duplicate refuse to overwrite keys it did not read.\n\nRelated: a plain PUT create picks up secrets left under a name, and deleting an Environment leaves its secrets behind (review P5). Evidence: ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261107-0247-decisions/review/redteam.md, the FX2-C5 report in run.md.","files":null}]}